h in these  situations  so this is only one of the many  applications of the rescue platform and  rna  in general where we can obviously  correct mendelian diseases or multiplex  to correct them  using the multiplexing capabilities of  cat 13  we can also modulate the catalysis or  post-translational states of  proteins and do this in a transient  fashion so this allows us to have  the precision of genome editing with  the uh kinetics and permanence of more  similar to other biologics or even small  molecules  so we only scratch the surface of what  these rna binding proteins can do  such as cast 13 inside the mammalian  cells so of course we can modulate  translation  or splicing or localization even  transcriptomics have been recent papers  using cast 13 for changing the m6a  states for example  and we see this toolbox is a rapidly  growing uh capability  maybe not as strong or as uh  full as the cast nine or dna targeting  toolbox but the only tool targeting  toolbox  is certainly getting there so to take it  back one  step to where we started yes natural  diversity  has been a risk resource resource of  course of crispr enzymes but also  other enzymes such as deaminases or  other genome modifying enzymes such as  integrases or recombinases so we're very  excited about using these and minding  these in a  comprehensive manner to find new tools  for  genome editing and translational  applications  so as omar mentioned  we're co-writing a lab together at the  montgomery institute now  um and we're excited about exploring  into  uh that natural diversity we'd also like  to thank everybody who was involved with  this  much of this work was done in zhang's  lab while we were graduate students  especially with david cox as well as  many other people who contributed  we're co-founders of sherlock  biosciences and advisor for beam  and you can check out our research at  hubbagoot.mnt.edu thanks for listening  and we're happy to take any questions  thanks so much  you
 

